# Every .env variant is a real secret file. `/.env` alone let two hand-made
# backups (.env.bak.localhost, .env.bak-before-localhost-origin) sit untracked-
# but-not-ignored, and one of them WAS committed. Ignore the family; the
# example is the one exception, and it holds names, never values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/dist
/node_modules
/src/scripts
/build_output.txt
/ticket_types.txt
